FerrionOS change to relibc (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 74b5e7e315043a21b599f271d5692727aa54f64d with the patches before it in the recipe's list applied:
- Close non-auxv upper-table handles in fexec_impl (same_process) and Sys::spawn so an exec'd or spawned program holds only the runtime handles exec gives it.
- In fexec_impl (same_process), open a temporary filetable-binary handle before arming current-addrspace and locking, hold FILETABLE.inner -> FILETABLE.fd across a bounded kernel table read (Refresh + lseek(0), bounded by CONTEXT_MAX_FILES), batch FileTableVerb::Close (with per-fd SYS_CLOSE fallback accepting EBADF only), and userspace table removal, failing closed on read, bound, or non-EBADF close errors.
- In Sys::spawn, scan the child's kernel file table through a separate temporary filetable-binary handle (never reading or seeking new_file_table, whose offset the child inherits) and close non-keep upper-table handles outside {child.thr_fd, proc_fd, ns_fd} alongside O_CLOEXEC descriptors before cloning new_file_table and cwd_fd, failing closed via ChildCleanupGuard.

